s($,"aXG","aHB",()=>A.b([A.ef("Hands are your scarcest thing. Post them to sheds in the harbour below; every hand eats each day and draws a wage whether or not it is working. Tap a shed to staff it.","welcome","You have the post",new A.atF()),A.ef("Ships buy what you have and sell what you lack. Selling in bulk drives that price down for days, so spread your trade around rather than dumping everything on one captain.","sell_first","A ship is at the quay",new A.atG()),A.ef("Every posted hand draws four coin a day whether or not the shed is earning. Nothing you make turns into coin until you sell it, so a port that never trades runs itself broke \u2014 and unpaid hands drift off to other crews. Send something out on the next ship.","wages","The purse is running down",new A.atH()),A.ef("Some of your people are not posted to anything. They still eat and still draw wages. Put them to work, or you are paying for nothing.","idle_hands","Idle hands",new A.atQ()),A.ef("A workshop runs at the rate of its scarcest input. If the sawmill has no timber, staffing it harder changes nothing \u2014 staff the forest camp that feeds it instead.","starved","A shed has nothing to work with",new A.atR()),A.ef("Sheds stack what they make in their own yard and wait for you. A full yard stops the shed \u2014 nothing is lost, but nothing more is being made. Tap it to collect, or build a warehouse: each one makes every yard half again as big.","yard_full","A shed has filled its yard",new A.atS()),A.ef("You cannot build everything yet. The Build panel lists what is still to come and the one thing that unlocks each \u2014 usually just raising the shed before it.","unlocks","The port grows into it",new A.atT()),A.ef("A full shed stops producing entirely. Sell it down, or build a warehouse. This is also the only thing that limits you while the app is closed \u2014 there is nothing to buy that raises it.","full_shed","A store is full",new A.atU()),A.ef("Raw timber pays 0.6c per worker-hour. Sawn into planks it pays nearly twice that, and the deeper chains pay better still. Every shed shows its rate on the Build tab.","refine","Refining beats selling raw",new A.atV()),A.ef("The ropewalk and the weaver both eat flax. The weaver pays more per worker; the ropewalk gets more out of each stalk. Which one you staff depends on whether hands or flax is your bottleneck today.","flax","The flax problem",new A.atW()),A.ef("You are holding more coin than you need. An Import Berth spends it by the hour on raw cargo \u2014 it is a rate you staff, not a shop. It only ever lands raws, so the finished goods still have to come out of your own sheds.","coin_idle","Coin is only worth what it buys",new A.atX()),A.ef("Under Trade there are captains and merchants for hire. A merchant raises every price you are paid; a captain makes voyages faster and safer. They cost coin to sign and a wage every day. (Your yards are carted in for you automatically as the port grows \u2014 no hire needed.)","hire","You can put people on the payroll",new A.atI()),A.ef("Selling on your own quay drives the price down. A voyage does not touch your local market at all \u2014 and each port pays for different things. The Trade panel shows which one pays best per day for whatever you have loaded.","voyages","Send your own cargo out",new A.atJ()),A.ef("Omens tell you exactly what is coming and for how long, and they do not lie. Use the time \u2014 stockpile, or move hands off whatever is about to stop working.","omen","That was a warning",new A.atK()),A.ef("The sound freezes in winter and nothing reaches the quay. It is the heaviest event in the deck and it happens every year, so it is worth building a stockpile before it arrives.","winter","Winter is a season, not an accident",new A.atL()),A.ef("People move in only when three things are true: a roof is free, there are two days of food in store, and the payroll is covered. Unpaid hands leave again, which is why a port can sit at the same number for days. Whichever one is missing is named under the HUD.","growth","Why the town is not growing",new A.atM()),A.ef("Every person eats one unit a day, fish first, then grain. Run out and a family leaves on the evening tide. Staff a farm or a wharf.","hungry","The stores are running down",new A.atN()),A.ef("Free traders will now call. They buy contraband and will swap it for materials at a rate coin cannot match. Everything you hold in plain sight is noticed \u2014 post hands to a bonded cellar to hide it.","dark_trade","You are in the dark trade now",new A.atO()),A.ef("Only what is exposed can be taken; concealed stock is safe, and no legitimate good is ever touched. You can scuttle it or declare it \u2014 both are free. Pausing costs nothing, so take your time.","cutter","A revenue cutter is standing by",new A.atP())],A.ao("z<Jf>")))
